quaydoc is importable as a library; every public name lives in a module with
a matching name.

## Parsing

```python
from quaydoc.parser import parse_document

document = parse_document(source_text, source="docs/index.qd")
for level, title in document.headings:
    print(level, title)
```

## Building a site

```python
from quaydoc.config import load_config
from quaydoc.site import Site

config = load_config("docs")
site = Site("docs", config).load()
stats = site.build(outdir="site")
print(stats.report())
```

## Checking a build

```python
from quaydoc.check import Checker

issues = Checker("site").check()
for issue in issues:
    print(issue.render())
```

## Templates

```python
from quaydoc.template import Template

template = Template("Hello, {{ name|upper }}!")
print(template.render({"name": "quaydoc"}))
```
